  "preamble": "Glottalization of the voiceless uvular stop [q] to the uvular ejective [qʼ]. Georgian renders Arabic ق /q/ with its uvular ejective ყ. Modern Georgian has no non-ejective uvular stop, because Old Georgian ჴ /qʰ/ merged with /x/. ყ is phonemically /qʼ/; Wiktionary transcribes it [χʼ], and Wikipedia describes [χʼ] as an allophone of /qʼ/. Georgian likewise renders Russian k, t and p with its ejectives (see the k > kʼ cell).",
